World "Intro"
Title "Introduction"

Introduction "Before we can verify real algorithms, we need to master the
basic moves: reading goals, introducing hypotheses, handling quantifiers and
connectives, assembling structured evidence, rewriting equalities, using
negation, and recursing on natural numbers. These thirteen short levels
establish the proof language every later world relies on."
